{"description": "Loads embedded RAG chunks into the vector store (upsert-first-then-delete-stale), updates the promoted CAS ledger and outputs a per-document load report; credentials come from the SAS Viya credential domain.", "displayName": "RAG - Load Vector Store.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [{"name": "_rgld_inventory", "displayName": "_rgld_inventory", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "type": "table", "id": "_rgld_inventory", "label": "_rgld_inventory"}], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgld_report", "displayName": "_rgld_report", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - Load Vector Store.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - Load Vector Store: load the embedded chunks (<project>_EMBEDDED)\n * into the vector store with upsert-first-then-delete-stale ordering (a\n * crash never leaves a document unretrievable), update the ledger\n * (<project>_LEDGER, promoted + saved) and output a per-document report.\n * Store credentials come from the SAS Viya credential domain - never from\n * the flow. Thin shell over rag_core.steps.run_load - see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgld_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgld_ragProject) %then %global _rgld_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgld_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgld_tablesCaslib;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgld_configHash) %then %global _rgld_configHash;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgld_history) %then %global _rgld_history;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgld_history)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgld_history = 1;\n%mend _rgld_setup;\n%_rgld_setup;\n/* Pipeline-wide state, shared by every RAG step in this session.\n   RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR: 1 (default) stops a SAS Studio Flow at the failing\n   step, which is what an interactive user wants. A SCHEDULED run sets it to\n   0: an aborted session never sends SAS Job Execution its completion\n   handshake, so the job would report running forever and its dead compute\n   server would keep counting against the context's server limit.\n   RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED: set by the step that fails; later steps then skip\n   their work and pass the inventory through, so the flow finishes tidily\n   instead of loading half a corpus. */\n%macro _rag_pipeline_state;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR) %then %do;\n        %global RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR;\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED) %then %global RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rag_pipeline_state;\n%_rag_pipeline_state;\n\n%let _rgld_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgld_rc = 1;\n%let _rgld_state = run;\n%let _rgld_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgld_summary = ;\n%let _rgld_nledger = 0;\n%let _rgld_nreport = 0;\n\n%macro _rgld_guard;\n    %if &RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED. NE 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgld_state = skip;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Load Vector Store: skipped - an earlier step of this run failed\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgld_guard;\n%_rgld_guard;\n%macro _rgld_inherit;\n    %global _rgld_runId;\n    %local dsid vproject vcaslib vrun rc;\n    %if %symexist(_rgld_inventory) %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgld_inventory)) NE 0 %then %do;\n        %if %sysfunc(exist(&_rgld_inventory.)) %then %do;\n            %let dsid = %sysfunc(open(&_rgld_inventory., i));\n            %if &dsid. NE 0 %then %do;\n                %let vproject = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., rag_project));\n                %let vcaslib = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., tables_caslib));\n                %let vrun = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., run_id));\n                %if %sysfunc(fetch(&dsid.)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n                    %if &vproject. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgld_ragProject = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vproject.));\n                    %if &vcaslib. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgld_tablesCaslib = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vcaslib.));\n                    /* the run id too: the lock belongs to the RUN, so a step\n                       that fails has to know which lock row to hand back */\n                    %if &vrun. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgld_runId = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vrun.));\n                %end;\n                %let rc = %sysfunc(close(&dsid.));\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n    /* a missing project is a failure of THIS step - but not when the step is\n       already skipping, where an absent inventory is expected */\n    %if &_rgld_state. EQ run %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgld_ragProject)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgld_state = fail;\n        /* one line: the value is embedded in a quoted putLog below, so a\n           newline inside it would break the string */\n        %let _rgld_error = the inventory does not name a RAG project - wire the output of RAG - List Documents into this step;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgld_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgld_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n%mend _rgld_inherit;\n%_rgld_inherit;\n%macro _rgld_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgld_report) %then %global _rgld_report;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgld_report)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgld_report = rgldout.&_rgld_ragProject._LOAD_REPORT;\n%mend _rgld_port_default;\n%_rgld_port_default;\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rgldout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rgldcas uuidmac=_rgld_casuuid;\n%let _rgld_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgld_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rgldout cas caslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rgldcas;\n\n%macro _rgld_export(portvar, file);\n    %if %symexist(&portvar.) %then %do;\n        %if %length(%superq(&&portvar.)) GT 0 %then %do;\n            %if %sysfunc(exist(&&&portvar..)) %then %do;\n                filename _rgld_io \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/&file.\";\n                proc json out=_rgld_io noSASTags;\n                    export &&&portvar..;\n                run; quit;\n                filename _rgld_io clear;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgld_export;\n%_rgld_export(_rgld_inventory, rgld_inventory_in.json);\n\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    # nothing to do when the step is only passing the inventory through\n    if str(SAS.symget(\"_rgld_state\") or \"run\").strip() != \"run\":\n        return\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGLOAD \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgld_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgld_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgld_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgld_backend\",\n        \"_rgld_collection\",\n        \"_rgld_storeHost\",\n        \"_rgld_storePort\",\n        \"_rgld_storeDb\",\n        \"_rgld_storeSslmode\",\n        \"_rgld_storeSsl\",\n        \"_rgld_deletedPolicy\",\n        \"_rgld_retainDays\",\n        \"_rgld_history\",\n        \"_rgld_credentialDomain\",\n        \"_rgld_embeddingDims\",\n        \"_rgld_configHash\",\n        \"_rgld_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgld_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgld_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def multiline(control):\n        \"\"\"Every line a user typed into a multi-line text field.\n\n        SAS Studio splits such a field for us: it emits <control>_count and\n        <control>_1..N, and leaves the plain macro variable holding only the\n        FIRST line. Reading just the plain one silently turned two questions\n        into one run-on question (found live in a flow). Semicolons are still\n        accepted, for callers that set the parameter directly.\n        \"\"\"\n        values = []\n        try:\n            count = int(float(SAS.symget(control + \"_count\") or 0))\n        except Exception:\n            count = 0\n        if count > 0:\n            for index in range(1, count + 1):\n                try:\n                    piece = str(SAS.symget(\"%s_%d\" % (control, index)) or \"\")\n                except Exception:\n                    piece = \"\"\n                if piece.strip():\n                    values.append(piece.strip())\n            if values:\n                return values\n        raw = str(P.get(control) or \"\").replace(\";\", \"\\n\")\n        return [line.strip() for line in raw.split(\"\\n\") if line.strip()]\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        try:\n            conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgld_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                            port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgld_casport\") or 5570)),\n                            password=TOKEN,\n                            session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgld_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # The step reuses the CAS session SAS created, because the staged\n            # table has to be visible to the casutil promote that follows. CAS\n            # only lets an identity reconnect to its OWN session, and a context\n            # that runs the server as a service account breaks that: SAS and\n            # its token are the service account while the CAS session belongs\n            # to the user who launched the job.\n            #\n            # SWAT's exception says only \"Could not connect ... on port 5570\";\n            # the server's real message (\"Users can only reconnect to their own\n            # sessions\") goes to stderr and never reaches the exception, so\n            # matching on text does not work. Connecting WITHOUT the session id\n            # separates the two causes: if that works, CAS is reachable and the\n            # problem is whose session it is.\n            reachable = False\n            try:\n                probe = swat.CAS(\n                    hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgld_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                    port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgld_casport\") or 5570)),\n                    password=TOKEN)\n                reachable = True\n                probe.close()\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            if reachable:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    \"this compute context cannot run the RAG steps: CAS is \"\n                    \"reachable, but the SAS session and the CAS session belong \"\n                    \"to different identities, so the step cannot reuse the CAS \"\n                    \"session it needs. The stock 'SAS Job Execution compute \"\n                    \"context' has this problem because it runs the server as a \"\n                    \"service account. Run the job in a context that runs as the \"\n                    \"REQUESTING USER - the 'SAS Studio compute context' does, \"\n                    \"and a full flow was verified there. See the RAG \"\n                    \"administration guide.\")\n            raise\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgld_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgld_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgld_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgld_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgld_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        def chunk_to_row(chunk):\n            row = dict(chunk)\n            for column in (\"span\", \"tags\", \"attributes\", \"entities\",\n                           \"relations\", \"embedding\"):\n                value = chunk.get(column)\n                row[column] = json.dumps(value) if value not in (None, \"\", {}) else \"\"\n            return row\n\n        def row_to_chunk(row):\n            chunk = dict(row)\n            chunk[\"chunk_index\"] = int(float(row.get(\"chunk_index\") or 0))\n            for column in (\"span\", \"entities\", \"relations\", \"embedding\"):\n                chunk[column] = json.loads(row[column]) if row.get(column) else None\n            chunk[\"attributes\"] = (json.loads(row[\"attributes\"])\n                                   if row.get(\"attributes\") else {})\n            chunk[\"tags\"] = json.loads(row[\"tags\"]) if row.get(\"tags\") else {}\n            for column in (\"heading_path\", \"prev_id\", \"next_id\", \"context_header\"):\n                chunk[column] = row.get(column) or None\n            return chunk\n\n        from rag_core.adapters import get_adapter\n        from rag_core.history import (EVENT_COLUMNS, EVENT_NUMERIC,\n                                      RUN_COLUMNS, RUN_NUMERIC)\n        from rag_core.credentials import fetch_secrets, store_config_from_secrets\n        from rag_core.steps import (INVENTORY_COLUMNS, LEDGER_COLUMNS,\n                                    check_config_drift, config_hash,\n                                    merge_config, merge_ledger,\n                                    record_history, run_load, stamp_config)\n\n        inventory_columns = INVENTORY_COLUMNS\n        missing = [name for name in (\"collection\", \"storeHost\", \"storeDb\")\n                   if not P[\"_rgld_\" + name]]\n        if missing:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"required parameters missing: \"\n                               + \", \".join(missing))\n\n        inventory = read_rows(\"rgld_inventory_in.json\",\n                              \"the inventory input port is not connected - \"\n                              \"wire the RAG - Embed Chunks updated-inventory \"\n                              \"output into this step\")\n        embedded = []\n        for row in cas_read(project_table(\"_EMBEDDED\")):\n            chunk = row_to_chunk(row)\n            if chunk.get(\"embedding\"):\n                embedded.append(chunk)\n\n        own_run_id = next((row.get(\"run_id\") for row in inventory\n                           if row.get(\"run_id\")), \"\")\n        ledger = []\n        for row in cas_read(project_table(\"_LEDGER\")):\n            ledger.append({column: (\"\" if row.get(column) is None\n                                    else row.get(column))\n                           for column in LEDGER_COLUMNS})\n        real_rows = [r for r in ledger if r.get(\"doc_id\") != \"__run_lock__\"]\n        # own_run_id is set by each step before this block: OUR run's lock is\n        # expected (the first step took it), anyone else's means a concurrent\n        # ingestion is live on this ledger\n        lock_rows = [r for r in ledger\n                     if r.get(\"doc_id\") == \"__run_lock__\"\n                     and str(r.get(\"run_id\") or \"\") != str(own_run_id or \"\")]\n        if lock_rows:\n            try:\n                held_for = time.time() - float(lock_rows[0].get(\"mtime\") or 0)\n            except Exception:\n                held_for = 1e9\n            if held_for < 1800:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"another ingestion run holds the lock on \"\n                                   \"this ledger - wait for it to finish, or \"\n                                   \"retry in 30 minutes if it crashed\")\n            M(\"stale run lock ignored (held longer than 30 minutes)\")\n\n        domain = P[\"_rgld_credentialDomain\"] or \"agentic-ai-keys\"\n        secrets = fetch_secrets(BASE, TOKEN, domain, verify=VERIFY)\n        if not secrets:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"no credential resolved from domain \" + domain\n                               + \" for this user - see the Managing \"\n                               \"Credentials administration guide\")\n        backend = P[\"_rgld_backend\"] or \"pgvector\"\n        # the TLS control depends on the backend: Postgres has six sslmode\n        # values, the MySQL-protocol stores only encrypted-or-not. A blank\n        # port follows the backend too (5432 vs 3306), in rag_core.env.\n        sslmode = (P[\"_rgld_storeSslmode\"] if backend == \"pgvector\"\n                   else (P[\"_rgld_storeSsl\"] or P[\"_rgld_storeSslmode\"]))\n        store_config = store_config_from_secrets(secrets, backend,\n                                                 P[\"_rgld_storeHost\"],\n                                                 P[\"_rgld_storePort\"],\n                                                 P[\"_rgld_storeDb\"],\n                                                 sslmode)\n        adapter = get_adapter(backend)\n        adapter.connect(store_config)\n\n        dims = 0\n        for chunk in embedded:\n            dims = len(chunk[\"embedding\"])\n            break\n        if not dims:\n            dims = int(float(P[\"_rgld_embeddingDims\"] or 0)) or 384\n        pipeline_version = \"v1\"\n        for row in inventory:\n            if row.get(\"pipeline_version\"):\n                pipeline_version = row[\"pipeline_version\"]\n                break\n\n        collection = P[\"_rgld_collection\"]\n\n        # complete the accumulated configuration, then hash it: this is the\n        # value stamped on the ledger AND on every chunk row\n        accumulated = \"\"\n        for row in inventory:\n            if row.get(\"config_json\"):\n                accumulated = row[\"config_json\"]\n                break\n        config_json = merge_config(accumulated, {\"backend\": backend,\n                                                \"collection\": collection})\n        configuration = P[\"_rgld_configHash\"] or config_hash(json.loads(config_json))\n\n        # refuse to mix two configurations into one collection (\u00a72b)\n        drift = check_config_drift(real_rows, configuration, pipeline_version)\n        if drift and not P[\"_rgld_configHash\"]:\n            raise RuntimeError(drift)\n\n        embed_model = \"\"\n        try:\n            embed_model = json.loads(config_json).get(\"embed_model\") or \"\"\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        deleted_policy = P[\"_rgld_deletedPolicy\"] or \"retire\"\n        retain_days = int(float(P[\"_rgld_retainDays\"] or 0))\n        load_stats = {}\n        # The Enrich step records the columns its stored outputs need in its\n        # own usage entry. This stage is the one holding the collection open,\n        # so it is where those columns are created and where the \"existing\n        # chunks are not backfilled\" note belongs.\n        enrich_schema = {}\n        for row in inventory:\n            try:\n                recorded = json.loads(row.get(\"enrich_usage\") or \"{}\")\n            except (ValueError, TypeError):\n                recorded = {}\n            if isinstance(recorded, dict) and recorded.get(\"attributes\"):\n                enrich_schema = recorded[\"attributes\"]\n                break\n        updated = run_load(embedded, inventory, adapter, collection,\n                           dims, pipeline_version, run_id=own_run_id,\n                           config_id=configuration, embed_model=embed_model,\n                           embed_dims=dims, deleted_policy=deleted_policy,\n                           retain_days=retain_days, attributes=enrich_schema,\n                           stats=load_stats, log=M)\n        total = adapter.count(collection)\n\n        # run history, beside the chunks: the ledger holds current state only\n        n_runs = n_events = 0\n        if P[\"_rgld_history\"] != \"0\":\n            written = record_history(\n                adapter, updated, real_rows, own_run_id, collection,\n                discovery=inventory,\n                config_id=configuration, settings=json.loads(config_json),\n                metrics={\"rag_project\": P[\"_rgld_ragProject\"],\n                         \"backend\": backend,\n                         \"pipeline_version\": pipeline_version,\n                         \"embed_model\": embed_model, \"embed_dims\": dims,\n                         \"collection_chunks\": total, **load_stats}, log=M)\n            # published to CAS so the history is reportable - the store stays\n            # authoritative, this copy is rebuildable\n            try:\n                from rag_core.history import History\n                reader = History(adapter.raw_connection(),\n                                 getattr(adapter, \"HISTORY_DIALECT\", \"postgres\"))\n                # the measures go up as numerics: a count staged as\n                # varchar is a CATEGORY in Visual Analytics and cannot be\n                # summed or multiplied by a price\n                n_runs = cas_stage(project_table(\"_RUNS\"),\n                                   [dict(r) for r in reader.runs(collection)],\n                                   RUN_COLUMNS, numeric=RUN_NUMERIC)\n                n_events = cas_stage(project_table(\"_DOC_EVENTS\"),\n                                     [dict(e) for e in reader.doc_events(collection)],\n                                     EVENT_COLUMNS, numeric=EVENT_NUMERIC)\n                M(f\"history published to CAS: {n_runs} runs, {n_events} events\")\n            except Exception as exc:\n                n_runs = n_events = -1\n                M(\"history not published to CAS: \" + str(exc)[:150])\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgld_nruns\", str(n_runs))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgld_nevents\", str(n_events))\n        adapter.close()\n\n        new_ledger = merge_ledger(real_rows, updated)\n        for row in new_ledger:\n            row[\"config_hash\"] = configuration\n        n_ledger = cas_stage(project_table(\"_LEDGER\"), new_ledger,\n                             LEDGER_COLUMNS, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n        stamp_config(updated, {\"backend\": backend, \"collection\": collection})\n        n_report = write_rows(\"rgld_report_out.json\", stamp(updated),\n                              inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgld_nledger\", str(n_ledger))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgld_nreport\", str(n_report))\n        statuses = {}\n        for row in updated:\n            statuses[row[\"status\"]] = statuses.get(row[\"status\"], 0) + 1\n        # statuses are the POST-load ones here (\"ingested\"), not the\n        # pre-load \"new\"/\"changed\" the inventory arrived with\n        loaded = sum(int(float(r.get(\"chunk_count\") or 0)) for r in updated\n                     if r.get(\"status\") == \"ingested\")\n        summarize(f\"{backend} collection {collection} on \"\n                  f\"{P['_rgld_storeHost']}/{P['_rgld_storeDb']}\")\n        summarize(f\"credentials resolved from domain {domain} \"\n                  f\"({backend.upper()}_RAG_USER)\")\n        summarize(f\"{len(embedded)} embedded chunks read from \"\n                  f\"{CASLIB}.{project_table('_EMBEDDED')} ({dims} dimensions)\")\n        summarize(f\"{loaded} chunks upserted for new or changed documents\")\n        summarize(\"documents: \"\n                  + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(statuses.items())))\n        summarize(f\"collection now holds {total} chunks\")\n        summarize(f\"stamped run {own_run_id}, configuration {configuration}\"\n                  + (f\", model {embed_model}\" if embed_model else \"\"))\n        summarize(\"previous chunk generations are retired, not deleted - the \"\n                  \"collection can be read as of an earlier date\")\n        summarize(f\"ledger {CASLIB}.{project_table('_LEDGER')}: \"\n                  f\"{n_ledger} documents\")\n        publish_summary(\"_rgld_summary\")\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgld_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgld_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgld_swap(suffix, count, persist=1);\n    %if &_rgld_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %if &count. LT 0 %then %return;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgldcas incaslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgld_ragProject.&suffix.\" quiet;\n        %if &count. GT 0 %then %do;\n            promote casdata=\"&_rgld_ragProject.&suffix._S\"\n                    casout=\"&_rgld_ragProject.&suffix.\";\n            %if &persist. EQ 1 %then %do;\n                save casdata=\"&_rgld_ragProject.&suffix.\"\n                     casout=\"&_rgld_ragProject.&suffix.\" replace;\n            %end;\n            %else %do;\n                /* not persisted by choice: clear any file an earlier run\n                   saved, or a restart would resurrect stale content */\n                deletesource casdata=\"&_rgld_ragProject.&suffix..sashdat\" quiet;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n        %else %do;\n            deletesource casdata=\"&_rgld_ragProject.&suffix..sashdat\" quiet;\n        %end;\n    quit;\n%mend _rgld_swap;\n%_rgld_swap(_LEDGER, &_rgld_nledger.);\n%_rgld_swap(_RUNS, &_rgld_nruns.);\n%_rgld_swap(_DOC_EVENTS, &_rgld_nevents.);\n%macro _rgld_passthrough;\n    %if &_rgld_state. NE skip %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgld_report., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgld_report., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgldout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgldcas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if %symexist(_rgld_inventory) %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgld_inventory)) NE 0 %then\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(&_rgld_inventory.)) %then %do;\n        data &_rgld_report.&opts.;\n            set &_rgld_inventory.;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgld_passthrough;\n%_rgld_passthrough;\n\n%macro _rgld_emit_report;\n    %if &_rgld_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgld_report., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgld_report., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgldout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgldcas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgld_nreport. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgldreo \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgld_report_out.json\";\n        libname rgldrej json fileref=rgldreo;\n        data &_rgld_report.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024\n                   embed_usage $ 256 enrich_usage $ 256;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\"\n                  embed_usage=\"Embedding usage (JSON)\"\n                  enrich_usage=\"Enrichment usage (JSON)\";\n            set rgldrej.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgldrej clear;\n        filename rgldreo clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgld_report.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024\n                   embed_usage $ 256 enrich_usage $ 256;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\"\n                  embed_usage=\"Embedding usage (JSON)\"\n                  enrich_usage=\"Enrichment usage (JSON)\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgld_emit_report;\n%_rgld_emit_report;\n%macro _rgld_release;\n    %local failing;\n    %let failing = 0;\n    %if &_rgld_state. EQ fail %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &_rgld_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgld_rc. NE 0 %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &failing. EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgld_runId) %then %return;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgld_runId)) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %sysfunc(exist(rgldout.&_rgld_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %return;\n    data rgldout.&_rgld_ragProject._LEDGER_R(replace=yes);\n        set rgldout.&_rgld_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(not (doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"\n                                 and run_id = \"&_rgld_runId.\")));\n    run;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgldcas incaslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgld_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgld_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        promote casdata=\"&_rgld_ragProject._LEDGER_R\"\n                casout=\"&_rgld_ragProject._LEDGER\";\n        save casdata=\"&_rgld_ragProject._LEDGER\"\n             casout=\"&_rgld_ragProject._LEDGER\" replace;\n    quit;\n    data _null_;\n        putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Load Vector Store: the run lock was released so the run can be retried\";\n    run;\n%mend _rgld_release;\n%_rgld_release;\n\nlibname rgldout clear;\ncas rgldcas terminate;\n\n%macro _rgld_status;\n    %if &_rgld_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgld_rc. NE 0 %then\n        %let _rgld_state = fail;\n    %if &_rgld_state. EQ skip %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Load Vector Store: skipped -----\";\n        run;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgld_state. EQ fail %then %do;\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 1;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"ERROR: RAG - Load Vector Store failed: %superq(_rgld_error)\";\n        run;\n        %if &RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR. NE 0 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                abort 42;\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    data _null_;\n        length part $ 500;\n        putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Load Vector Store -----\";\n        do i = 1 to countw(\"%superq(_rgld_summary)\", \"|\");\n            part = strip(scan(\"%superq(_rgld_summary)\", i, \"|\"));\n            if part ne \"\" then putLog \"NOTE:   \" part;\n        end;\n    run;\n%mend _rgld_status;\n%_rgld_status;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Loads the embedded chunks (<project>_EMBEDDED) into the vector store and finalizes the run: new chunks are upserted FIRST, stale ones deleted after, then the ledger (<project>_LEDGER) is updated, promoted and saved. Vector store credentials are resolved from the credential domain as <BACKEND>_RAG_USER / <BACKEND>_RAG_PW - secrets never appear in the flow.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_inventory\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"inputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Updated inventory (from RAG - Embed Chunks):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_collection\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Collection (lowercase identifier, e.g. rag_hr_policies_v1):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_storeHost\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store host:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_storePort\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store port (blank = the backend default: 5432 pgvector, 3306 singlestore):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_storeDb\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Database name:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"pgvector\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"pgvector (PostgreSQL)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"singlestore\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SingleStore\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_storeSslmode\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SSL mode:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"disable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"disable\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"allow\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"allow\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"prefer\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"prefer\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"require\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"verify-ca\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"verify-ca\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"verify-full\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"verify-full\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgld_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pgvector\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_storeSsl\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"TLS:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"require (TLS)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"disable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"disable (no TLS)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgld_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"singlestore\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_credentialDomain\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Credential domain:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_history\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Run history (rag_runs / rag_doc_events beside the collection, published to CAS for reporting):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"1\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Record this run\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"0\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Do not record\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_deletedPolicy\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"When a document disappears from the source:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"retire\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Keep its chunks as history (retired, not retrieved)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"purge\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Remove its chunks permanently, history included\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_retainDays\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"numstepper\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Keep retired chunk generations for this many days (0 = keep them forever):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"integer\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"min\": 0,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"max\": null,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"stepsize\": 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_embeddingDims\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"numstepper\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Embedding dimensions (0 = take them from the data; only used when creating an empty collection):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"integer\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"min\": 0,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"max\": null,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"stepsize\": 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgld_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgld_report\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Per-document load report output:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - Load Vector Store step\\n==========\\n\\nTerminates the RAG ingestion flow: per-document upsert-then-retire-stale into the vector store (backends: pgvector (PostgreSQL), SingleStore), tombstoning of deleted documents, then the merged ledger is promoted AND saved so incremental ingestion survives server restarts. The report output shows every document's final status.\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents \u2192 Extract Text \u2192 Chunk Documents \u2192 Embed Chunks \u2192 Load Vector Store. The bulk data travels beside the flow in promoted CAS tables named <project>_ELEMENTS, <project>_CHUNKS, <project>_EMBEDDED and <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib (each saved to disk, so state survives server restarts; names stay within 32 characters so they display nicely in SAS Studio). Each step's output table lands in that same caslib as <project>_INV_LIST, _INV_EXTRACT, _INV_CHUNK, _INV_EMBED and <project>_LOAD_REPORT unless you point the output port somewhere else. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages (swat/pandas carry the pipeline tables to CAS - varchar columns, no 32k limit).\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\\n* psycopg2-binary for the pgvector (PostgreSQL) backend.\\n* singlestoredb for the SingleStore backend.\\n* A credential domain (default agentic-ai-keys) holding <BACKEND>_RAG_USER/<BACKEND>_RAG_PW entries (authored from your .env by the create-credential-domain script) - see the Managing Credentials guide in the Administration documentation.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Documentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Do not run this flow while the scheduled Ingest-Documents job is active on the same ledger - the step refuses when it sees a fresh run lock.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.2 (29JUL2026)\\n      - SAS Content document sources; output tables land in the tables caslib; labelled columns; numeric and list-of-values fields; run summary in the log\\n* Version: 1.1 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Pipeline tables move to promoted CAS tables via SWAT (varchar, no 32k limit); automatic embed checkpoint\\n* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgld_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgld_collection\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgld_storeHost\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgld_storePort\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgld_storeDb\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgld_backend\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"pgvector\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"pgvector (PostgreSQL)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgld_storeSslmode\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"prefer\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"prefer\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgld_storeSsl\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"require (TLS)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgld_history\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"1\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Record this run\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgld_deletedPolicy\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"retire\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Keep its chunks as history (retired, not retrieved)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgld_retainDays\": 0,\n\t\t\"_rgld_credentialDomain\": \"agentic-ai-keys\",\n\t\t\"_rgld_embeddingDims\": 0\n\t}\n}"}